1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,930
Do you have a job?
你有工作吗？

2
00:00:01,930 --> 00:00:10,270
If you do, you'll know the world of work can be tough – long hours, tedious tasks and stress.
如果有的话，你就会知道身处职场实属不易——工作时间长、任务单调乏味，还充满压力。

3
00:00:10,270 --> 00:00:17,910
But it can bring benefits too, such as a regular salary and, sometimes, job satisfaction.
但工作也能带来不少好处，比如稳定的薪水，有时还能收获职业成就感。

4
00:00:17,910 --> 00:00:25,580
Maybe that's why more of us are now taking on a side hustle – another name for a second job.
或许这就是为什么现在越来越多的人开始做起了副业——也就是兼职的另一种说法。

5
00:00:25,580 --> 00:00:33,570
For some having two jobs is a necessity – a way to make ends meet and provide extra income.
对一些人来说，身兼两职是迫不得已的选择——这是一种维持生计、赚取额外收入的办法。

6
00:00:33,570 --> 00:00:41,340
But it now seems that more people want to put their skills and passions into practice to make money.
但如今，似乎更多人是为了发挥自身技能、追逐个人爱好来赚钱。

7
00:00:41,340 --> 00:00:50,040
These tend to be entrepreneurial young people who want to work on their own projects alongside their main source of income.
这类人群往往是富有创业精神的年轻人，他们希望在主业之外，经营属于自己的项目。

8
00:00:50,040 --> 00:01:01,300
According to Henley Business School, around one in four workers run at least one side hustle business, half of which were started in the past two years.
据亨利商学院统计，大约四分之一的职场人士至少经营着一份副业，其中半数副业是在过去两年内开启的。

9
00:01:01,300 --> 00:01:11,270
Those aged 25 to 34 are most likely to be involved, with 37% thought to run a sideline of some kind.
25至34岁的人群参与副业的概率最高，约37%的该年龄段人群都有一份副业。

10
00:01:11,270 --> 00:01:18,810
It calculates that the average side hustler makes about 20% of their income through their second job.
数据显示，副业从业者平均约20%的收入来自于副业。

11
00:01:18,810 --> 00:01:26,880
But what's interesting is that many millennials are turning their hand to new jobs not just for money and security.
但有趣的是，许多千禧一代开始尝试新工作，并非仅仅为了金钱和稳定。

12
00:01:26,880 --> 00:01:34,460
Research has found that almost three-quarters of people are following a passion or exploring a new challenge.
研究发现，近四分之三的人是在追寻爱好，或是挑战全新领域。

13
00:01:34,460 --> 00:01:48,520
BBC News spoke to Becci Mai Ford, who works some of the time for a telecommunications company to pay the bills, but spends the rest of her time developing her crafting company Ellbie Co.
英国广播公司新闻频道采访了贝琪·麦·福特，她在一家电信公司兼职赚钱维持生计，其余时间则用来发展自己的手工艺品公司埃尔比公司。

14
00:01:48,520 --> 00:01:57,870
She says going full-time is "not financially worth it right now but it fuels my creative soul and makes me happy."
她表示，现在全职经营副业“在经济上并不划算，但这能满足我的创作热情，让我感到快乐。”

15
00:01:57,870 --> 00:02:04,450
Mobile apps have also aided the more commercially minded side hustler.
各类手机应用也为那些有商业头脑的副业从业者提供了助力。

16
00:02:04,450 --> 00:02:19,390
Peer-to-peer firms such as Uber, Deliveroo, Airbnb and TaskRabbit allow users to do everything from odd jobs to renting out homes and parking spaces from their mobile phone.
优步、户户送、爱彼迎和跑腿兔等点对点服务平台，让用户可以通过手机完成各种业务，从零散的跑腿活儿到出租房屋、停车位，一应俱全。

17
00:02:19,390 --> 00:02:30,610
Of course having a side hustle means you are self-employed - or freelance - which can give you flexibility to work when you like, but it can be risky.
当然，做副业意味着你属于个体经营者——或者说是自由职业者，这种工作模式能让你灵活安排工作时间，但同时也存在风险。

18
00:02:30,610 --> 00:02:37,390
You sometimes work on a zero-hours contract and may not get offered enough work.
你可能会签订零时工合同，面临工作量不足的问题。

19
00:02:37,390 --> 00:02:42,270
Or what was originally your passion may become more of a chore.
或者，曾经热爱的事业，也可能慢慢变成枯燥乏味的琐事。

20
00:02:42,270 --> 00:02:50,600
However, this could be the best way to try out a new career or follow a passion while not giving up the day job.
不过，在不放弃主业的前提下，副业或许是试水新职业、追逐个人爱好的最佳途径。
